  "text": "Telephones: MF 4848 - MF 4849\nCommonuealth Public Seruire Clerical Angoriation\n(Registered as an Organisation under the Conciliation and Arbitration Act)\nGENERAL SECRETARY\nG. W. F. SMITH, LL.B.\nCENTRAL EXECUTIVE\nTELEGRAPHIC CODE ADDRESS\n\"CLERICAL,\" MELBOURNE.\nGWS: EM\nPLEASE QUOTE IN REPLY\n12/3.\nV.C.A. BUILDING,\n1 COLLINS PLACE,\nMELBOURNE, C.1.\n9th June, 1955•\nc.E. McFadyen, Esq., C.B.E.,\nSecretary,\nDepartment of Shipping & Transport,\n497 Collins Street,\nMELBOURNE•\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nI should like to extend to you,\non behalf of the\nAssociation and myself, sincere\ncongratulations on the\nhonour which has been conferred on you.\nThe award to you of the C.B.E. will no doubt give\nsatisfaction, not only\nto officers\nyour own Department\nwith whom you are\ndirectly associated, but also to\nofficers generally.\nI am sure it will afford no small measure of\nsatisfaction to yourself that your services have received\nrecognition in this manner.\nYours sincerely,\n(GEO. W.F. SMITH)\nGENERAL SECRETARY•\nI WAS FiRST PRESIDENT ANT EXECUTIVE COUNCiLLOR OF THE\nFEDERMA CAPITRA TERRITORY BRANCH OF THE CP.SCA. HATING\nWor AuToNomy FOR THE TERRITORY AT THE AMMURL MEETING\nOR THE FERERAL EZECUTIVE IN MERBOURNE IN 1924. PRIOR TO THAT\nDATE WE WERE A SECTIONAL COMMITTER OF THE MSH. BOnY.\nF.C.MEERe WAS THe FIRST SECRETARY. He HAS LATER KNIGHTER AS\nCOmPTROLLER GENERAL REDS. CUSTOMS • EXCISE",
